{"availability":"available","full":"VictorButoi/FleXray","name":"FleXray","description":"FleXray: Universal Clinical X-ray Segmentation","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":98,"forks":15,"created":"2026-09-22T23:12:51Z","updated":"2026-09-23T05:28:40Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://flexray.csail.mit.edu/","topics":["ai","computer-vision","machine-learning","medical-imaging","segmentation"],"demo":"https://flexray.csail.mit.edu/#demo","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:22.347Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:22.347Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T04:14:22.347Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T18:00:15.948Z","stars":93,"forks":13},{"at":"2026-10-13T04:14:22.347Z","stars":98,"forks":15}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Victor Ion Butoi, Vivek Gopalakrishnan, John V. Guttag, Adrian V. Dalca, Neel Dey","FleXray (pip package flexray, imported as fxr) is a command-line tool and Python package for segmenting anatomy in X-ray images. The quickest path is to install the package, run flexify on an image or folder of images, and inspect the saved NumPy arrays.","FleXray can also train new full-body X-ray segmentation models. Training combines 2D X-ray segmentation data (including generated/FluXray samples) with CT segmentation volumes rendered to DRRs during training."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VictorButoi/FleXray/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a9ec20270dad16a498ec4c9804bb7a7613dc684850490d69200729d52871e527","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:16.122Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:00:16.122Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Victor Ion Butoi, Vivek Gopalakrishnan, John V. Guttag, Adrian V. Dalca, Neel Dey","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VictorButoi/FleXray/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a9ec20270dad16a498ec4c9804bb7a7613dc684850490d69200729d52871e527","sourceUrl":"https://g